By the Law of Cosines on triangle $O_1 O_3 O_2$,
\[r^2 = x^2 + 4\cdot4^2 - 4 \cdot 4 \cdot x \cos \angle O_1 O_2 O_3.\]
By the Law of Cosines on triangle $O_2 O_3 O_1$,
\[r^2 = (5-x)^2 + 3^2 - 3 \cdot 3\dot (5-x) \cos \angle O_2 O_1 O_3.\]
Setting the right hand sides of these two equation equal and solving the resulting quadratic in $x$ gives $x = 1$.
